  "selection": "Declared sample of one opening-grammar generator on three carriers: the N=3 complete graph (3 edges), a 5-node chain (4 edges), and a 5-node cycle (5 edges). Lengths are 0, 5, 9 and 12, plus length 10 on the chain only. Not an exhaustive grammar grid. Not a grid in which every long list sits on three edges. Not scheduled to explain PAT-005, PAT-006, PAT-007, or the line-graph identity. The incident predicate is not in this round. Composition operators are not in this round.",
  "construction": "The menu has eight templates, in order: prohibit either when the condition is present; multiply by 2 either when present; multiply by 3 either when absent; prohibit form when present; multiply by 5 either when present; prohibit dissolve when absent; multiply by 4 either when absent; prohibit either when absent. Template i mod 8 is applied at position i. The event is carrier edge i mod m. The condition is edge (i mod m + 1 + i // m) mod m, or the next edge when that index is the event. Baseline is 1. Length 0 is the empty list. Cardinality counts constraints. It is not a node-count target.",
